    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93817" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημει-ώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>remarkable,
			conspicuous</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.1.3
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); of language, <i>peculiar, singular</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνόματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Isoc.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>significant</i> of something to come, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					373a30
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Vent.</u>
				35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐνύπνια ἔχει τι ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Div.Somn.</u>
				462b15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.286b
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δῶς</span>
			<i>remarkably</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.2.28
			</span></i>.</div>
